To achieve your goal of prioritizing routes based on the lowest total internal cost (MED) across different partner networks, configure the following BGP best-path settings:

```cli
configure router bgp best-path-selection
    always-compare-med infinity
    deterministic-med
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `always-compare-med infinity` forces BGP to compare MED values for all routes, even if they originate from different neighbor ASes. Missing MEDs are treated as infinity (least preferred), ensuring paths without cost metrics are deprioritized.  
- `deterministic-med` guarantees consistent best-path selection by grouping routes by neighbor AS before MED comparison, eliminating path selection dependency on route arrival order.  

This configuration ensures BGP always prefers the path with the lowest summed MED value across all partner networks.
