To ensure only basic BGP communities are advertised to the legacy neighbor and block extended/large communities (including bandwidth-related ones), use the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    group "LEGACY_GROUP"
        neighbor <legacy_IP>
            disable-communities extended large
```

**Key Details:**  
- Replace `"LEGACY_GROUP"` with your BGP group name and `<legacy_IP>` with the neighbor's IP.  
- The command `disable-communities extended large` removes 8-byte extended communities (e.g., bandwidth attributes) and 12-byte large communities from updates sent to this neighbor.  
- Standard 4-byte communities (e.g., traffic engineering tags) are preserved.
