Replace `<neighbor-ip-address>` with the peer's IP address and `<arbitrary-as>` with a dummy AS number (e.g., `64512`). The `private` option hides the local AS in received paths, while `no-prepend-global-as` prevents your true backbone AS (`65535`) from appearing in advertised paths. This ensures the peer never sees your real AS details in routes.
