## Proposed answer:
To adjust the BGP keepalive interval to 60 seconds, use the following commands. Ensure the hold-time is set to at least 180 seconds (3x the keepalive) for stability:

**Global Configuration:**
```cli
configure router bgp
    keepalive 60 hold-time 180
    exit
```

**Per Group:**
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    keepalive 60 hold-time 180
    exit
```

**Per Neighbor:**
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    keepalive 60 hold-time 180
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` and `<ip-address>` with your specific group and neighbor details. This ensures peers receive keepalives every 60 seconds while maintaining session stability.
