To configure the router to respect bandwidth metrics for BGP traffic steering and prefer routes with higher-capacity links, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group "EBGP_GROUP"
            link-bandwidth
                aggregate-used-paths ipv4
            exit
```

### Explanation:
1. **`link-bandwidth`**: Enables processing of the link-bandwidth extended community attached to BGP routes. This is applied under the BGP group (e.g., `EBGP_GROUP`) where routes with bandwidth metrics are received.
2. **`aggregate-used-paths ipv4`**: Aggregates bandwidth values from the link-bandwidth extended communities of used multipaths for IPv4 routes. This ensures the router advertises the aggregated bandwidth to peers (when using `next-hop-self`), influencing path selection toward higher-capacity links.

Replace `EBGP_GROUP` with your BGP peer group name. If supporting IPv6, add `ipv6` to the command (e.g., `aggregate-used-paths ipv4 ipv6`).
