To restrict BGP next-hop resolution to specific tunnel types, configure a resolution filter under the BGP next-hop resolution settings. Here are the CLI commands:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            shortcut-tunn
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        sr-te
                        sr-ospf
                    exit
                exit
            exit
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family ipv4
                        resolution-filter
                            sr-te
                            sr-ospf
                        exit
                    exit
                exit
            exit
```

**Key details:**  
- This filter explicitly allows only `sr-te` (Segment Routing Traffic Engineered) and `sr-ospf` (Segment Routing OSPF) tunnels.  
- Any tunnel types **not** listed in the resolution filter (e.g., LDP, RSVP) will be ignored for BGP next-hop selection.  
- Replace `ipv4` with `ipv6` if working with IPv6 routes.  
- To modify the allowed tunnels, add or remove `sr-te`/`sr-ospf` under `resolution-filter`.  

> **Note**: The tunnel types in the filter override all other preferences. Only the explicitly listed tunnel types will be considered.
